    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "Direct follow-up fixes have been COMMITTED to this same PR branch (current head `78d56ce6098856082047486806663406a83fb954`): (1) Core now tracks live Stage7.15 Oleg escape vote timers with a runtime WeakMap and exposes `resumeStage715OlegEscapeVote`; unlike a saved numeric `_escapeTimer`, this can restart after real browser reload while guarding duplicate timers. (2) Stage7.15 controller `unlockOlegEscapeBattle()` re-arms Core during `oleg_escape_vote` resume. (3) The rendered DOM test no longer fabricates the first failed outcome or clears Core timers: it waits for actual controller `failed` then `success`, asserts actual 2:3 / 3:2 and REP and money debits. JS syntax for changed controller, core and DOM test parsed. All Web/docs pairs remain identical. \n\nSTILL BLOCKED: the Oleg escape success card's generic `Закрыть` suppression is not yet fixed; `ui-battles.js` still computes `stage715OlegNoPostLossActions` only for the first-loss `isStage715OlegScriptedBattle`, not for `isStage715OlegEscapeBattle`. The exact required one-line patch is:\n\n`const stage715OlegNoPostLossActions = (isStage715OlegScriptedBattle(b) || isStage715OlegEscapeBattle(b)) && b.meta.stage715OlegNoPostLossActions === true;`\n\nApply it in **both** Web/docs `ui-battles.js`, then run the full real Chromium DOM script from the PR head in the Codex worktree (`node tools/test_stage7_15_atom6_oleg_escape_dom.mjs`), fix any genuine failures, and add reload-while-voting checkpoints, final DM/System dialogue assertions, and ledger idempotency checks. GitHub PR checks do not currently execute the Chromium script, so green checks alone are insufficient. Do not merge until full real lifecycle evidence passes. User does not need to relay any instructions.",
