    "body": "## Summary\n\nRestores the scripted Oleg escape battle after the first Oleg DM reply and after a failed escape. The card keeps the canonical prompt and three scripted yellow choices, preserves the same battle ID, and exposes only “Уйти”. The Oleg scripted choices are isolated from generic choice generation/cache paths.\n\nThe escape controller seeds each Oleg attempt before calling the existing escape API. A narrowly metadata-gated Oleg attempt nonce lets the two authorized payments use distinct idempotency keys; generic escape contexts remain unchanged. Web/docs mirrors and cache tokens are updated.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Rendered-DOM Chromium regression: PASS for exact prompt, three yellow choices, only “Уйти”, generic cache poisoning/invalidation, scripted answer routing, repeated click protection, same battle identity, 2:3 then 3:2 attempt configuration, and two total money charges.\n- Stage 7.15.31 escape contract, Atom 5 Oleg first-loss, Oleg DM, Rayhan reveal/result/post-win, demo isolation/routing: PASS.\n- JavaScript syntax, Web/docs byte parity, git diff --check: PASS.\n- test_stage7_15_50_progressive_disclosure.py still fails on its pre-existing assertion for a missing telemetry(\"stage715_oleg_battle_result\") marker in watchOleg; the marker is absent on the exact base and outside this change.\n- The DOM harness does not establish reload checkpoints or the completed vote settlement/DM sequence. No Safari acceptance is claimed.\n\nNo merge requested.",
